      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Nubhotepet|852889\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"The transliteration Nb-ḥtp reads as the signs n, b, ḥ, t, p. In Nubhotepet, n is matched by N, b by b, ḥ by h, t by the t after 'o', and p by p. The vowel letters u, o and e stand for no sign, which is allowed. That leaves the final t of Nubhotepet unmatched, because every sign of the transliteration is already used and the transliteration has no t after p. The rules allow a feminine t to be omitted from record 1, not added to it. Record 1 therefore has a consonant the transliteration lacks, so the spelling stands for a different name (a feminine Nb-ḥtp.t) rather than Nb-ḥtp.\"}"
